===== scripts/failure_atlas_v2/restart_monitor.py =====
     1	"""Restart-Mixture Monitor (RMM): an attachable recovery wrapper for deployment policies.
     2	
     3	Weakness addressed
     4	------------------
     5	Certificate methods (Gated deployment, DISCERN, SMCS) accumulate evidence over all history and
     6	stop acquiring once a verdict fires; posterior/weight methods (Model Picker, CAMS, Gong-Zhang)
     7	accumulate cumulative losses. Either way a change after early evidence is answered slowly or
     8	never: a late improvement is diluted by the early regime, and a reversal after promotion is never
     9	rolled back because nothing is being measured.
    10	
    11	Decision rule
    12	-------------
    13	Let X_n = s_n * D_{tau_n} be the n-th queried disagreement outcome (label clock, no inverse
    14	propensity weight), signed so that X_n = +1 means the NON-deployed model was right (s_n = +1 if
    15	model 0 is deployed, -1 otherwise). For bet sizes lambda in a fixed grid Lambda and a fixed grid
    16	of label start indices S (every ``gap`` labels), the detector is
    17	
    18	    M_n = (1/|Lambda|) sum_{lambda in Lambda} sum_{s in S, s <= n} pi_s prod_{k=s}^{n} (1 + lambda X_k),
    19	
    20	with pi_s = 1/|S|. On M_n >= 1/alpha_k the wrapper switches deployment and RESTARTS the base
    21	policy on the remaining horizon and budget with the newly deployed model as its incumbent; the
    22	detector is reset with alpha_{k+1}. Promotions (switching to the challenger, model 1) spend
    23	alpha_det / 2^j on the j-th promotion alarm; rollbacks to model 0 use alpha_rb.
    24	
    25	The wrapper also keeps acquiring after the base stops, with the same budget pacer the base uses,
    26	so the detector always has labels; these labels are not shown to the base.
    27	
    28	Validity. Under the uniform conditional null that the challenger is never better on
    29	disagreements, each product from a start s is a nonnegative supermartingale (it is constant 1
    30	before s), so V_n = M_n + sum_{s in S, s > n} pi_s is a nonnegative supermartingale with V_0 = 1
    31	and Ville gives P(sup_n M_n >= 1/alpha) <= alpha. The base runs at alpha_base, so the total
    32	probability of any challenger promotion under that null is at most alpha_base + alpha_det.
    33	Delays: outcomes enter in event order, after release, exactly as in the base adapters.
    34	"""
    35	
    36	from __future__ import annotations
    37	
    38	import math
    39	import sys
    40	from pathlib import Path
    41	
    42	import numpy as np
    43	
